-- DRAFT for owner review. Not applied.
-- Rebuilds Michigan county figures from ACS 2020-2024 5-year files (tables B19013 and B03002), data year 2024.
-- Why: the stored 2024 county median household incomes do not match the ACS 2024 file (12 of 12 counties
-- checked differ by 1-4%, e.g. Wayne 59,521 stored vs 60,539 in the file). Population already matches.
-- Places (Adrian, Detroit, Warren) and ZCTAs (48201, 48226, 48072, 49931) were checked and already match.
-- Block 1: median household income and its margin of error (new column; "*****" in the file = no margin, stored NULL).
-- Block 2: Black population count and share, from B03002 "Black or African American alone, not Hispanic or Latino"
--          (share = count / total population x 100, rounded to 2 decimals, calculated here at load time).
--          The stored shares (Wayne 37.20, Macomb 12.50) do not match the 2024 file (36.56, 12.70). Run block 2 only
--          if you accept this definition; the card text must then say "not Hispanic or Latino".

